1
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:04,870

2
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:08,880
Welcome, everybody. Welcome to Amazing Discoveries.

3
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:11,590
Oh, oh! It's on again.

4
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:14,630
Guys, could we please not watch this?

5
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:18,180
Folks, this ever happen to you? You go to get a nice glass of milk...

6
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:21,640
...but these darn cartons are so flinging, flanging hard to open.

7
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:23,770
Boy, you said it, Mike.

8
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:30,020
- There's gotta be a better way.     - And there is, Kevin.

9
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:33,440
- Can we please turn this off?     - No way, Kevin.

10
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:37,360
What if I told you there's a new product that guarantees...

11
00:00:37,530 --> 00:00:40,490
...you'll never have to open up milk cartons again?

12
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:42,910
Meet the Milkmaster 2000.

13
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:47,790
- Intrigued?     - You're flinging, flanging right I am.

14
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:51,050
This is his first time. He's never used this.

15
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:54,050
You're gonna see how easy this is to do.

16
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:58,010
- This works in any milk carton.     - Wow, it is easy. Ha, ha.

17
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:00,600
Now I can have milk every day.

18
00:01:09,500 --> 00:01:14,000
# So no one told you life was gonna be this way #

19
00:01:14,570 --> 00:01:18,740
# Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. #

20
00:01:19,650 --> 00:01:23,460
# It's like you're always stuck in second gear #

21
00:01:23,920 --> 00:01:26,020
# When it hasn't been your day, #

22
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:29,020
# your week, your month, or even your year #

23
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:32,980
# but I'll be there for you #

24
00:01:32,980 --> 00:01:34,810
# When the rain starts to pour #

25
00:01:34,810 --> 00:01:37,930
# I'll be there for you #

26
00:01:37,930 --> 00:01:39,770
# Like I've been there before #

27
00:01:39,770 --> 00:01:42,780
# I'll be there for you #

28
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:46,440
# 'Cause you're there for me too #

29
00:01:53,780 --> 00:01:56,240
It's official. There are no good movies.

30
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:58,990
So let's go to a bad one and make out.

31
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:08,080
Perhaps you would like me to turn like this so you can bunny-bump against my back?

32
00:02:09,870 --> 00:02:10,870
- Hey.     - Hey.

33
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:13,920
- Hey, man. What's up?     - Maybe you can tell me.

34
00:02:14,170 --> 00:02:17,880
My agent would like to know why I didn't show up at my audition today...

35
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:21,930
...the first good thing she gets me in weeks. How could you not give me the message?

36
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:24,510
I'll tell you, I do enjoy guilt...

37
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:26,810
...but it wasn't me.

38
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,930
Yes, it was. It was him. Uh-huh.

39
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:32,230
Okay, it was me.

40
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:37,730
- How was it you?     - Well, it was all so crazy, you know?

41
00:02:37,990 --> 00:02:40,990
Chandler was in the closet counting to 10 and was up to seven...

42
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:43,160
...and I hadn't found a place to hide yet.

43
00:02:44,490 --> 00:02:48,950
Look, I meant to tell you, and I wrote it all down on my hand. See? All of it.

44
00:02:49,410 --> 00:02:51,250
- Yep, that's my audition.     - Yeah.

45
00:02:51,540 --> 00:02:54,420
See? Now, this is why I keep notepads everywhere.

46
00:02:54,590 --> 00:02:57,500
Yep. And that's why we don't invite you to play.

47
00:02:58,590 --> 00:03:02,090
What is the great tragedy here? Get yourself another appointment.

48
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:06,390
Well, Estelle tried. The casting director told her I missed my chance.

49
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:07,810
Well, that is unfair.

50
00:03:07,970 --> 00:03:10,640
I'll call her. I'll tell her it was totally my fault.

51
00:03:10,850 --> 00:03:13,770
You can't. The casting director doesn't talk to friends.

52
00:03:13,980 --> 00:03:17,270
- She only talks to agents.     - What a sad little life she must lead.

53
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,780
Okay. Ooh.

54
00:03:20,950 --> 00:03:24,570
- What are you doing? What are you doing?     - No, I know, I know. Ooh.

55
00:03:25,070 --> 00:03:28,330
Hi, this is Caitlin from Phoebe Buffay's office.

56
00:03:28,490 --> 00:03:32,250
Um, is, um, Anne there for Phoebe?

57
00:03:32,420 --> 00:03:34,750
She'll know what it's about.

58
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:36,880
Hang up. Hang up right...

59
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:41,970
Annie? Hi. Listen, we've got a problem with Joey Tribbiani.

60
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:45,680
Apparently, he missed his audition. Who did you speak to in my office?

61
00:03:45,970 --> 00:03:48,260
Estelle? I don't know what I'm gonna do with her.

62
00:03:48,430 --> 00:03:52,640
So your husband leaves and burns down the apartment. The world does not stop.

63
00:03:53,810 --> 00:03:55,400
Is anybody else scared?

64
00:03:56,980 --> 00:04:00,900
If Joey loses this audition, then that is it for Estelle. I don't care.

65
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:04,570
Annie, you are a doll. What time can you see him?

66
00:04:04,740 --> 00:04:06,870
I need a pen. Pen.

67
00:04:12,660 --> 00:04:16,580
Get the woman a pad. Get the woman a pad. A pad! A pad!

68
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:19,420
Oh, now you want a pad.

69
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:24,050
- Hey.     - Hello.

70
00:04:24,220 --> 00:04:26,220
Where's my boy?

71
00:04:26,390 --> 00:04:28,510
Here's my boy.

72
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:32,470
And here's his Barbie.

73
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:39,770
What's, uh...? What's my boy doing with a Barbie?

74
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:43,530
He picked it out at the toy store himself. He loves it.

75
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,360
He carries it everywhere, like a security blanket.

76
00:04:46,530 --> 00:04:49,570
But with ski boots and a kicky beret.

77
00:04:50,490 --> 00:04:52,200
Yeah, it's cute.

78
00:04:52,370 --> 00:04:55,370
Why does he have it again?

79
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:58,540
So he's got a doll. So what?

80
00:04:59,380 --> 00:05:02,920
Unless you're afraid he's gonna grow up to be...

81
00:05:03,090 --> 00:05:04,720
...in show business.

82
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:09,050
This wouldn't have to do with the fact that he's being raised by two women?

83
00:05:11,100 --> 00:05:16,060
You know what? It's fine. If you're okay with the Barbie thing, so am I.

84
00:05:16,230 --> 00:05:19,520
Give Daddy the Barbie. Give me the Barbie. Okay, how about...?

85
00:05:19,730 --> 00:05:22,070
Don't you wanna play with a monster truck?

86
00:05:24,150 --> 00:05:25,400
No? Okay.

87
00:05:25,570 --> 00:05:28,320
Ooh, ooh. How about a Dino-Soldier?

88
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:35,500
You are so pathetic.

89
00:05:35,660 --> 00:05:39,120
Why can't your son just play with his doll?

90
00:05:45,420 --> 00:05:47,090
I gotta go to work.

91
00:05:48,760 --> 00:05:50,470
Has anybody seen my left boob?

92
00:05:52,470 --> 00:05:54,100
I loved that movie.

93
00:05:58,270 --> 00:06:00,270
Here it is. Joey, what are you doing?

94
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:03,150
I'm sorry. It just felt nice.

95
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:08,530
Joe. Joe. Answer the phone.

96
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:12,280
I only got one arm. You should do stuff for me. Get me a sweater.

97
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:15,450
Just do it. It's Janice.

98
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:17,620
And if I get it, I'm gonna have to see her tonight.

99
00:06:20,290 --> 00:06:22,670
Oh, that's great. I'm gonna have to see her tonight.

100
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:25,130
Why don't you wanna see Janice?

101
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:27,550
Last night at dinner, when the meals came...

102
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:32,470
...she put half her chicken piccata on my plate and took all my tomatoes.

103
00:06:34,390 --> 00:06:36,520
And that's bad...

104
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,980
...because you hate chicken piccata?

105
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:40,810
No.

106
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:45,360
You didn't wanna share your tomatoes. Tomatoes are very important to you.

107
00:06:45,530 --> 00:06:47,480
All of a sudden, we were this couple.

108
00:06:47,690 --> 00:06:50,320
And this alarm started going off in my head.

109
00:06:50,490 --> 00:06:52,660
"Run for your life! Get out of the building!"

110
00:06:53,660 --> 00:06:55,910
Ugh. Men are unbelievable. Janice thought she was giving you chicken.

111
00:06:56,160 --> 00:06:57,700
What is it with you people?

112
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:00,910
The minute you feel something, you have to run away?

113
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,330
I know. That...

114
00:07:04,670 --> 00:07:09,130
That's why I don't wanna go tonight. I'm afraid I'm gonna say something stupid.

115
00:07:09,340 --> 00:07:12,180
Oh. You mean that guy thing where you act mean and distant...

116
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:14,550
...until you get us to break up with you?

117
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,930
Hey, you know about that?

118
00:07:17,850 --> 00:07:19,520
What do I do? I wanna get past this.

119
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:22,020
I don't wanna be afraid of the commitment thing.

120
00:07:22,190 --> 00:07:25,690
I wanna go through the tunnel to the other side.

121
00:07:26,690 --> 00:07:29,940
Where there's no fear of commitment.

122
00:07:30,110 --> 00:07:32,070
Do we have any...?

123
00:07:36,370 --> 00:07:37,910
Do we have any thoughts here?

124
00:07:38,450 --> 00:07:40,500
I've never been through the tunnel myself because...

125
00:07:40,660 --> 00:07:43,330
...you're not allowed through with more than one girl in the car.

126
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:51,170
But it seems to me it's pretty much like anything else. Face your fear.

127
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:54,380
You have a fear of heights? Go to the top of the building.

128
00:07:54,550 --> 00:07:56,550
You're afraid of bugs.

129
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:58,430
Get a bug.

130
00:07:59,640 --> 00:08:01,060
Right?

131
00:08:01,230 --> 00:08:02,980
You have a fear of commitment.

132
00:08:03,230 --> 00:08:07,690
So I say you go in there and you be the most committed guy there ever was.

133
00:08:07,860 --> 00:08:10,110
Amazingly, that makes sense.

134
00:08:10,990 --> 00:08:14,070
- Do you think?     - Oh, yeah. Go for it, man.

135
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:15,410
Jump off the high dive.

136
00:08:15,570 --> 00:08:19,240
Stare down the barrel of the gun. Pee into the wind.

137
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,460
Joe, if I'm staring down the barrel of a gun...

138
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:26,710
...I'm gonna be pretty much peeing every which way.

139
00:08:28,750 --> 00:08:31,210

140
00:08:31,960 --> 00:08:33,590
Ooh, it's your audition from this morning.

141
00:08:34,970 --> 00:08:36,010
Can I use the phone?

142
00:08:36,180 --> 00:08:39,800
Sure, that's what it's there for. Emergencies and, uh, pretend agents.

143
00:08:41,810 --> 00:08:43,810
Come on, baby. Come on.

144
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:48,440
Hi. I have Phoebe Buffay returning a page.

145
00:08:48,610 --> 00:08:52,190
Okay, well, she's in her car. I'll have to patch you through.

146
00:08:52,360 --> 00:08:54,030
Very nice touch.

147
00:08:55,450 --> 00:08:56,660
Okay, go ahead.

148
00:08:58,240 --> 00:09:00,370
Talk, talk, talk.

149
00:09:00,540 --> 00:09:02,330
Hi, Annie?

150
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:03,830
Fantastic.

151
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,330
- You got it.     - Oh! You got it.

152
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:09,290
Um, will he work for scale, you ask me?

153
00:09:09,460 --> 00:09:10,670
Well, I don't know about that.

154
00:09:10,840 --> 00:09:13,460
Except that l do and he will.

155
00:09:14,170 --> 00:09:16,550
Great. Oh, you are such a sweetheart.

156
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:19,140
I would love to have lunch with you.

157
00:09:19,300 --> 00:09:22,140
How about we have lunch next...?

158
00:09:22,310 --> 00:09:24,390
Oop, went through a tunnel. Ha, ha.

159
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:25,680
Unbelievable.

160
00:09:25,850 --> 00:09:27,890
Oh, thank you so much.

161
00:09:28,060 --> 00:09:32,690
It was really fun. I mean, I've never talked on a car phone before.

162
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:36,110
Oh. You are so amazing. Could you do me this huge favor?

163
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:39,780
There's this one other audition I want, and Estelle couldn't get me in.

164
00:09:39,990 --> 00:09:42,490
Uh, I don't know. It was fun one time, but...

165
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:45,160
Come on, please? It would just be this one more.

166
00:09:45,330 --> 00:09:46,830
Well, actually it's two.

167
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,160
- Two?     - Yeah.

168
00:09:48,330 --> 00:09:49,870
Well, really it's three.

169
00:09:50,330 --> 00:09:54,090
Please? You're so good at it. I love you.

170
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:56,760
Okay. But just these three, right?

171
00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:58,220
No, it's four.

172
00:10:02,680 --> 00:10:04,850
So how come you wanted to eat in tonight?

173
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:07,730
Because I wanted...

174
00:10:07,890 --> 00:10:09,520
...to give you this.

175
00:10:09,690 --> 00:10:14,440
Oh. Are you a puppy!

176
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,570
Contact paper.

177
00:10:21,030 --> 00:10:24,030
You never know what to say when someone you're sleeping with...

178
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,950
...gives you contact paper. Ha, ha.

179
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:30,920
Wait, there's more. See, the contact paper is to go...

180
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:33,960
...in your brand-new drawer.

181
00:10:36,050 --> 00:10:38,380
See, the drawer actually goes in my dresser.

182
00:10:38,590 --> 00:10:42,090
Oh. You didn't have to do this.

183
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,760
Yes, I did.

184
00:10:43,930 --> 00:10:46,470
Yes, I did. Because you're my girlfriend...

185
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:50,060
...and that's what girlfriends should get.

186
00:10:50,690 --> 00:10:54,060
Oh. Well, I gotta buy a vowel...

187
00:10:55,730 --> 00:10:59,440
...because, oh, my God. Mwah.

188
00:10:59,610 --> 00:11:01,780
Who would've thought that someday...

189
00:11:01,990 --> 00:11:05,080
...Chandler Bing would buy me a drawer?

190
00:11:06,450 --> 00:11:08,450
Well, not me.

191
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:13,460
But that's what's happened. And, uh, there's more.

192
00:11:14,750 --> 00:11:16,420
We should take a trip.

193
00:11:17,090 --> 00:11:18,090
We should?

194
00:11:18,260 --> 00:11:21,090
Yup. We're a couple, and that's what couples do.

195
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:23,800
And I wanna meet your parents.

196
00:11:23,970 --> 00:11:26,810
We should take a trip with your parents.

197
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:36,310
I don't think we need to, because you're tripping me out right now.

198
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:38,730
- Are you okay?     - No, I am.

199
00:11:38,900 --> 00:11:41,320
Ha, ha. I actually am. This is amazing.

200
00:11:41,530 --> 00:11:44,780
My entire life, I have feared this place.

201
00:11:45,030 --> 00:11:47,740
And now that I'm here, it's like, what was the big deal?

202
00:11:47,910 --> 00:11:51,790
I could probably say, "Let's move in together," and I'd be okay.

203
00:11:52,290 --> 00:11:54,620
You probably want us to move in together?

204
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:59,050
- It doesn't scare me.     - Yeah, well it scares me.

205
00:11:59,210 --> 00:12:03,130
I'm not even divorced yet. You just invited me over here for pasta...

206
00:12:03,300 --> 00:12:06,300
...and all of a sudden you're talking about moving in together.

207
00:12:06,470 --> 00:12:08,560
And I wasn't even that hungry.

208
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:12,680
You know what? It's getting really late, and I should just, um...

209
00:12:12,850 --> 00:12:15,850
Don't go. I've scared you. I've said too much.

210
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:19,070
I'm hopeless and awkward and desperate for love.

211
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,990
Hey, Janice, it's me.

212
00:12:29,490 --> 00:12:33,410
I wanted to apologize in advance for having chased you down the street.

213
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:35,370
Bye-bye.

214
00:12:40,340 --> 00:12:42,630
Here you go, honey. This will help.

215
00:12:43,470 --> 00:12:45,470
So I catch up to her and she says...

216
00:12:45,630 --> 00:12:48,090
...this relationship's going too fast and we have to slow down.

217
00:12:48,260 --> 00:12:51,010
gh. That is never good.

218
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:52,970
Then I got all...

219
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:55,690
...needy and clingy.

220
00:12:55,850 --> 00:12:59,610
Now, wait a minute. Maybe it's not so bad. How did you leave it?

221
00:12:59,770 --> 00:13:00,820
She said she'd call me.

222
00:13:04,150 --> 00:13:05,240
Oh, God.

223
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:08,740
Ugh. Welcome to our side of the tunnel.

224
00:13:09,530 --> 00:13:11,830
This ice cream tastes like crap, by the way.

225
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:15,620
Yeah, well, it's that low-cal, nondairy, soy-milk junk.

226
00:13:15,790 --> 00:13:18,750
We save the real stuff for the truly terminal cases.

227
00:13:19,540 --> 00:13:23,170
When you start getting screwed over all the time, you gotta switch to low-fat.

228
00:13:23,340 --> 00:13:25,260
Yeah, you do.

229
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:27,680
So you don't think I'm terminal?

230
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:32,100
Oh, no, not at all. You're not terminal. We just need some damage control.

231
00:13:32,260 --> 00:13:34,140
Okay. Okay. So should I call her?

232
00:13:34,310 --> 00:13:36,060
No.

233
00:13:37,060 --> 00:13:40,730
It's a critical time. If you feel yourself reaching for that phone...

234
00:13:40,900 --> 00:13:43,400
...you go shopping, you get your butt in a bubble bath.

235
00:13:43,570 --> 00:13:47,150
If you want her back, you have got to start acting aloof.

236
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:49,410
She has to know you're not needy.

237
00:13:49,570 --> 00:13:51,370
So, what you have to do is...

238
00:13:51,530 --> 00:13:54,490
...you have to accidentally run into her on purpose...

239
00:13:54,660 --> 00:13:56,500
...and then act aloof.

240
00:13:58,170 --> 00:14:00,750
So I'm not gonna lose her?

241
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:03,500
Oh, honey, you're not a total loser.

242
00:14:07,090 --> 00:14:09,260
I said, so I'm not gonna lose her?

243
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:18,180
Guess who's here.

244
00:14:18,440 --> 00:14:21,400
It's the toughest guy in Toyland, Ben.

245
00:14:21,610 --> 00:14:25,650
Real American hero I'm G.I. Joe

246
00:14:25,820 --> 00:14:28,320
Drop the Barbie. Drop the Barbie.

247
00:14:28,530 --> 00:14:32,120
G.I. Joe? You really think he's gonna fall for that?

248
00:14:33,370 --> 00:14:36,740
G.I. Joe? Cool. Can I play?

249
00:14:38,460 --> 00:14:42,250
Look, Ben. It's a toy that protects U.S. Oil interests overseas.

250
00:14:42,420 --> 00:14:44,500
Go, Joe!

251
00:14:45,670 --> 00:14:46,960
Hello. Oh.

252
00:14:47,130 --> 00:14:49,380
- Phoebe, there you are.     - No, it's not. Sorry.

253
00:14:49,550 --> 00:14:52,300
But, Phoebe, wait, wait. Phoebe. Phoebe.

254
00:14:52,470 --> 00:14:55,600
Oh, Joey. Oh, okay. See, I didn't recognize you...

255
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:57,350
...in those pants.

256
00:14:59,230 --> 00:15:01,640
That TV movie I went in for, did you hear anything?

257
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:03,610
I think I got a shot at it.

258
00:15:03,770 --> 00:15:05,520
Yes, they called. You didn't get it.

259
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:10,610
Okay? I mean, you didn't get it. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

260
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:13,280
That's okay. These things happen.

261
00:15:13,450 --> 00:15:16,280
But they shouldn't happen. You know what?

262
00:15:16,490 --> 00:15:18,620
You're in a terrible, terrible business.

263
00:15:19,870 --> 00:15:23,420
I don't wanna be the person who makes your face look like that. Ugh.

264
00:15:23,630 --> 00:15:26,420
I'm okay. See?

265
00:15:27,250 --> 00:15:29,840
Now you're sad and creepy.

266
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:32,630
You know what? I'm sorry. I quit, okay?

267
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:36,470
No, no, no, you can't quit. You're the best agent I ever had.

268
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:40,180
Look, rejection is part of being an actor. You can't take it personal.

269
00:15:40,430 --> 00:15:43,420
Not personal? They said they'd never met an Italian actor

270
00:15:43,630 --> 00:15:45,020
with a worse Italian accent.

271
00:15:45,610 --> 00:15:47,150
They actually said that?

272
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:51,320
Yeah. Oh, God, there's that face again. See? I can't do this job.

273
00:15:51,490 --> 00:15:53,740
No, this is why you have to do this job.

274
00:15:53,910 --> 00:15:55,110
Agents always lie.

275
00:15:55,320 --> 00:15:58,280
Estelle just says stuff like, "They went another way."

276
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:00,330
But this? I can use this.

277
00:16:00,540 --> 00:16:03,370
I can work on a new accent.

278
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:07,500
Yeah, okay. No. If it helps you, okay. Yeah.

279
00:16:07,710 --> 00:16:11,130
You'll never get me, Joe!

280
00:16:24,190 --> 00:16:26,020
No, thank you.

281
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:29,820
Chandler.

282
00:16:30,230 --> 00:16:32,320
Hello, Janice.

283
00:16:34,570 --> 00:16:36,860
What are you doing here?

284
00:16:37,030 --> 00:16:38,830
Uh, just a bit of shopping.

285
00:16:38,990 --> 00:16:40,870
How have you been?

286
00:16:41,910 --> 00:16:44,410
Are you being British?

287
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,080
No.

288
00:16:46,250 --> 00:16:48,250
Not anymore.

289
00:16:48,710 --> 00:16:52,050
Why are you shopping here? You don't live in this neighborhood.

290
00:16:52,210 --> 00:16:54,260
Were you here waiting for me?

291
00:16:58,390 --> 00:17:00,050
I'm just, uh, you know...

292
00:17:00,220 --> 00:17:02,680
...picking up some things for a party.

293
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:06,390
Barley?

294
00:17:06,560 --> 00:17:08,690
What kind of a party serves barley?

295
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:11,980
Well, I'm sorry if my friends aren't as sophisticated as yours.

296
00:17:13,570 --> 00:17:15,950
- Where is this party?     - Here in Chelsea.

297
00:17:16,490 --> 00:17:17,910
Whose party is it?

298
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:20,450
- A woman's.     - What woman?

299
00:17:21,950 --> 00:17:23,700
Chelsea.

300
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:28,420
Either you're seeing somebody behind my back...

301
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:31,250
...which would make you the biggest jerk on the planet...

302
00:17:31,420 --> 00:17:33,670
...or you're pretending you're seeing somebody...

303
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:37,510
...which just makes you so pathetic I could just start crying right here.

304
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:41,260
So which of these two guys do you wanna be?

305
00:17:42,310 --> 00:17:44,470
Can I be that guy?

306
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:50,900
Okay, we got some more good rejections. Lots of stuff to work on.

307
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:53,230
Oh. Okay. Shoot.

308
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:56,110
Okay. Um... Oh, the zoo commercial.

309
00:17:56,320 --> 00:17:57,530
- I didn't get it?     - No.

310
00:17:57,700 --> 00:18:01,660
They said that you "weren't believable as a human being."

311
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:05,580
So you can work on that.

312
00:18:05,750 --> 00:18:07,540
Great. What else?

313
00:18:07,710 --> 00:18:11,670
Um, the off-Broadway-play people said that you were "pretty but dumb."

314
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:14,170
No, wait, I'm sorry. That's "pretty dumb."

315
00:18:14,340 --> 00:18:18,010
Oh. Look, it's okay, no, no, no. Really.

316
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:19,510
Look, um...

317
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:22,300
...I really appreciate this, Pheebs...

318
00:18:22,470 --> 00:18:24,890
...but I'm gonna have to go back to Estelle.

319
00:18:26,270 --> 00:18:28,680
Don't get me wrong. You're a better agent than she is...

320
00:18:28,850 --> 00:18:32,730
...but at least with her, I don't wanna blow my pretty dumb brains out.

321
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:35,940
Yeah, no, I understand.

322
00:18:36,110 --> 00:18:37,820
- You do? Thanks. Okay.     - Yeah.

323
00:18:37,990 --> 00:18:39,610
Sorry.

324
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:44,030
- Wait a minute.     - What?

325
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:45,450
Wait a minute.

326
00:18:45,660 --> 00:18:49,080
Did you just make all that stuff up to get out of being my agent?

327
00:18:49,250 --> 00:18:51,620
Oh, he caught me.

328
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:54,210
I am so busted.

329
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:58,590
That's what I suspected.

330
00:19:01,720 --> 00:19:04,050
And then I just, you know...

331
00:19:04,470 --> 00:19:08,220
...threw the bag of barley at her and ran out of the store.

332
00:19:08,390 --> 00:19:12,730
My God, Chandler, we said be aloof, not a doof.

333
00:19:13,810 --> 00:19:17,230
I've actually ruined this, haven't I?

334
00:19:18,190 --> 00:19:20,320
It's time for the good ice cream now, right?

335
00:19:20,990 --> 00:19:22,820
- Yeah, it is.     - Okay.

336
00:19:22,990 --> 00:19:26,200
You know what? Everything's gonna be okay.

337
00:19:29,410 --> 00:19:30,450
Hello?

338
00:19:31,370 --> 00:19:33,040
Hi, Janice.

339
00:19:33,210 --> 00:19:34,920
Can you hold on for a second?

340
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:36,750
Okay. Okay.

341
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:38,050
What do I do?

342
00:19:38,210 --> 00:19:40,170
I don't know. This is unprecedented.

343
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:43,050
If we ever did what you did, a man would never call.

344
00:19:43,220 --> 00:19:44,260
Hello?

345
00:19:44,430 --> 00:19:47,430
I got it. Pretend you just woke up. That'll throw her off.

346
00:19:47,640 --> 00:19:49,770
- Be sleepy.     - Yes. And grumpy.

347
00:19:50,020 --> 00:19:52,640
What are you...? Stop naming dwarves.

348
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:57,770
Hello, Janice. Hi.

349
00:19:57,940 --> 00:20:00,570
I'm so glad that you called.

350
00:20:01,780 --> 00:20:06,200
I know I've been acting really weird lately...

351
00:20:07,530 --> 00:20:10,580
...and it's just because I'm crazy about you...

352
00:20:13,250 --> 00:20:17,420
...and I just got stupid and scared...

353
00:20:17,590 --> 00:20:19,550
...and stupid a couple more times.

354
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:21,880
And I'm sorry.

355
00:20:23,380 --> 00:20:24,930
Really?

356
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:28,430
Ha, ha. Really?

357
00:20:28,600 --> 00:20:30,930
He's so lucky. If Janice were a guy...

358
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:33,940
...she'd be sleeping with somebody else by now.

359
00:20:35,230 --> 00:20:36,520
I love you too.

360
00:20:36,690 --> 00:20:38,400
Ugh. It's so unfair.

361
00:20:46,490 --> 00:20:48,780
G.I. Joe? G.I. Joe?

362
00:20:48,950 --> 00:20:52,790
Hey, I don't know what to tell you guys. That's the doll he chose.

363
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:55,500
What'd you do, dip it in sugar?

364
00:20:55,750 --> 00:20:58,130
Look, G.I. Joe's in, Barbie's out.

365
00:20:58,290 --> 00:21:01,710
And if you guys can't deal with it, that's just your too bad.

366
00:21:03,670 --> 00:21:07,640
What are you being such a weenie for? So he has a Barbie. Big deal.

367
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:09,930
You used to dress up like a woman.

368
00:21:16,020 --> 00:21:17,770
What?

369
00:21:17,940 --> 00:21:20,270
The way you used to dress up in Mom's clothes?

370
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:22,360
What are you talking about?

371
00:21:22,610 --> 00:21:25,530
The big hat, the pearls, the little pink handbag?

372
00:21:25,820 --> 00:21:28,360
Okay. You are totally making this up.

373
00:21:28,870 --> 00:21:30,870
How can you not remember?

374
00:21:31,030 --> 00:21:32,740
You made us call you "Bea"?

375
00:21:39,380 --> 00:21:41,170
Oh, God.

376
00:21:41,710 --> 00:21:45,260
I've literally never been this happy.

377
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:47,550
Wasn't there a little song?

378
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:50,180
Oh, please, God, let there be a song.

379
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:52,560
There was no song. There was no song.

380
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:54,140
I am Bea

381
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:56,390
- I drink tea...     - That's enough.

382
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:57,980
Won't you?

383
00:21:59,350 --> 00:22:00,770
Won't you?

384
00:22:01,480 --> 00:22:02,770
Won't you?

385
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:06,860
Won't you dance around with me?

386
00:22:13,200 --> 00:22:16,000
I am Bea

387
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:18,870
I drink tea

388
00:22:19,040 --> 00:22:23,630
Won't you dance around with...?

389
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:35,600
Ross!

